# Pull and benchmark run logs. Timestamped, noisy in diffs, and regenerable by
# re-running the script that wrote them. The measured data (results/*.tsv and
# the tables in the documents) is committed instead — same convention as
# ../ollamaClaudeCode_v1 and ../ollamaClaudeCode_v2.
*.log
*.log.done
results/*.log
results/*.log.done

# cc-session fixture working trees. Each is its own throwaway git repository
# rebuilt from scratch by cc-session.sh on every run, so committing them would
# nest a repo inside this one and freeze a regenerable artefact. The transcript
# (cc-*.jsonl), the verdict table (cc-session.tsv) and the inspected diffs in
# measurements.md are the evidence that is kept.
results/cc-*/

# sandbox: the built image is not a repo artefact; results are.
sandbox/*.log

# report.html is generated by make-report.py from results/*.tsv. Committed
# anyway (v3 committed its report.html too): it is the artifact people are sent,
# and having it in history shows what was claimed at each point.

# Terminal-Bench: the built toolchain image is not a repo artefact; task
# definitions, verifiers, solutions and results are. Per-run agent transcripts
# under results/tb/ are regenerable, like the cc/ ones.
results/tb/
